
---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our Water · Our Source</div>
      <h1>Pure ambition.<br />Natural origins.</h1>
      <p>
        Our journey begins at a natural spring in Belgut, Kenya.
        We are working towards responsible spring-water production,
        guided by water-quality testing and a commitment to
        protecting the source.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/conservation/">
          Our conservation approach
        </a>
        <a class="btn alt" href="/contact/">
          Explore a partnership
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="water-status">
        Preparing for launch · Commercial bottling has not yet begun
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
<!-- Watercana: Our Water Photo -->
<section class="water-photo-section">
  <div class="water-photo-container">
    <img
      src="/images/watercana-our-water.png"
      alt="Watercana spring water surrounded by the natural green landscape of Belgut, Kenya"
      class="water-photo"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="water-photo-caption">
    <span class="water-photo-eyebrow">
      OUR WATER
    </span>

    <h2>
      Pure by Nature, Protected for Generations.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Our journey begins with a natural spring
      in Belgut, Kenya, where our commitment
      to responsible water sourcing and
      environmental conservation takes root.
    </p>

    <strong>
      Conservation with every sip.
    </strong>
  </div>
</section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">The beginning</div>
      <h2>Water begins at the source.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        We believe responsible water production begins with
        understanding and protecting the natural environment
        that supplies it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Watercana is developing a spring-water enterprise built
        around a natural freshwater source in Belgut. Our
        preparations include source protection, preliminary
        water-quality analysis and planning for a treatment
        and bottling facility.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Quality and transparency</div>
      <h2>Testing today. Preparing for tomorrow.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Our first laboratory analysis was conducted by
        Davis &amp; Shirtliff in January 2026.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Initial analysis</h3>
          <p>
            The laboratory examined physical and chemical
            characteristics of water sampled from the spring,
            providing a baseline for our planning.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Areas requiring attention</h3>
          <p>
            The initial analysis identified pH and total
            suspended solids as outside the guideline
            values referenced in the report.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Further verification</h3>
          <p>
            Microbiological testing, appropriate treatment,
            and finished-water verification remain necessary
            before commercial drinking-water production.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="water-note">
        These are preliminary source-water findings,
        not certification of drinking-water safety.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Preparing for launch</div>
      <h2>Building a responsible water business.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Our next phase is to establish the infrastructure,
        processes and quality controls needed to bring
        Watercana to market.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>01 · Processing facility</h3>
          <p>
            Establish a suitable water-treatment and bottling
            facility, informed by the source-water analysis
            and applicable regulatory requirements.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>02 · Product quality</h3>
          <p>
            Complete further testing, validate treatment
            performance and implement appropriate quality
            assurance procedures before commercial release.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>03 · Responsible distribution</h3>
          <p>
            Develop bottled-water distribution alongside
            planned refillable supply solutions for schools
            and institutions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Our difference</div>
      <h2>More than a bottle of water.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Watercana is designed to connect a commercially
        sustainable water business with long-term
        environmental stewardship.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our business model commits 20% of future net
        profits to natural spring protection, indigenous
        reforestation and community environmental awareness.
      </p>
      <a class="btn dark" href="/conservation/">
        Discover our conservation model
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Be part of the journey</div>
      <h2>Help us bring responsible spring water to market.</h2>
      <p>
        We welcome conversations with potential institutional
        customers, technical partners and early-stage supporters.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .water-status {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .water-note {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .water-note,
  .water-status {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section .wrap > p {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .section .card p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
